<title>UK: UK M0 grows provisional 7.5 pct in year to Oct.</title>
<headline>UK M0 grows provisional 7.5 pct in year to Oct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England released the following provisional data on M0 money supply -</p>
<p>    MONEY SUPPLY (in pct)	  OCTOBER	    SEPTEMBER</p>
<p>    M0 in month (adjusted)	  +0.7		+0.2</p>
<p>    M0 annual (adjusted)	    +7.5		+7.0</p>
<p>    M0 annual (unadjusted)	  +7.5		 +7.2</p>
<p>NOTE - consensus forecast was 0.5 percent month-on-month, 7.1 percent yr/yr s/adj growth.</p>
<p>The Bank of England said notes and coins in circulation rose a seasonally adjusted 0.4 percent month/month and 7.4 percent year-year.  </p>
<p>    M0 in month (unadjusted) 0	     -1.2</p>
<p>-- Richard Murphy, London Newsroom 44 171 542 2774</p>
</text>
